OL,3,ASpain train disaster clouds Sanchez
OL,4,Achances of re-election
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe breaking news from Spain this week
OL,7,Fwas shocking but also shockingly
OL,8,Ffamiliar: another collision on the
OL,9,Fhigh-speed rail line south from Madrid,
OL,10,Fwith reports of dozens killed.
OL,12,FIt is just nine months since two trains
OL,13,Fcrashed near Cordoba, killing 46
OL,14,Fpeople. Now 69 bodies have been
OL,15,Frecovered here in central Spain, from
OL,16,Fwreckage strewn over the tracks and
OL,17,Fdown an embankment.
OL,19,FFor the victims' families it is
OL,20,Fdevastating; a personal tragedy.
OL,23,APub: 31-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
FL,316,300,200,140,0,100
